              "text": "Any of these actions (even if they require multiple cards) may be initiated as long as there is at least one card in the targeted deck or pile. If there are an insuffi cient quantity of cards in the deck or pile to complete the action, simply complete what is possible and then end the action. An empty Reserve Deck does not stop you from drawing destiny, that destiny draw simply fails (see 1. F. Failed Destiny Draws) An empty Force Pile does not prevent a player from using \"0 Force\" or his \"entire Force Pile.\" An empty Lost Pile does not stop a player from initiating an action that retrieves Force (or retrieves card(s)). An empty Force Pile does not stop a player from moving that pile, such as placing it on an empty or non-empty Used Pile, with I Did It! An empty deck or pile does not stop a player from placing a card or cards under that deck or pile.",
