        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 12,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Section B. Taking Cards From A Deck/Pile",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Many cards allow you to directly access your deck, pile, or stack, usually to take a card into hand, play a card, or to deploy a card from there directly. Whenever a card or rule allows you to take, play, deploy, exchange, relocate, retrieve, reveal, search for, etc. a card from a deck, pile or stack, and there are any criteria for what kind of card you may take, you must reveal that card after it is obtained (reveal the entire card) regardless of initial face-down or face-up orientation. In this way, your opponent can check that you took a card matching the criteria specified. However, when allowed to take \"",
              "bold": false,
