        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 12,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If your search fails to find any card matching the criteria given, your opponent is permitted to look through that deck, pile, or stack in order to prove that no candidate could have been taken; this is called \"verifying. \" An exception to this is that an opponent may not verify your hand; however, they may call a judge to verify your hand for them. In addition, when the card or card type you searched for was not found and your opponent has verified this, you may not use that search function (even if on a card with the same name) to search or look through the same deck, pile, or stack again this turn.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
