          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Starting The Game",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Starting the game consists of two steps:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Step A",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Playin gstarting cards",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "There are five types of starting cards:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Starting Effects: Each player may choose one Starting Effect from his deck.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Starting location: A single location a player chooses to start the game. You may choose any location so long as it can meet any deployment conditions (see Starting Location).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Objective: Type of card that represents long-term planning by providing specific starting cards, game play conditions, and short and long term rewards for completing tasks. (See Ch. 9 for detailed info rmation on Objectives). A player who has an Objective card in his deck must start with it (on the 0 side) and may not have more than one. A player has either a starting location or an Objective, never both.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Starting Interrupt: Each player may choose one Starting Interrupt from his deck.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Cards that may not be placed into your Life Force.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "These are cards other than Objectives which are deployed at the start of game either by an Objective or via their own game text which include the stated restriction clause.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "While these cards (along with any or all of the cards they permit or require) may legally be revealed in any order, either player may insist that both players adhere to the following sequence:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "1. Both players simultaneously reveal their Starting Effect, if any, then resolves his Starting Effect now.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 35,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "After resolving your starting effect, unless otherwise instructed, any cards that that state \" reveal to opponent",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "He may not voluntarily change an",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
