              "text": "undercover spies prevent drains from being initiated Light controls the Endor system and the Light Endor wherever they are; Boushh isn't canceling the drain, sites Bunker and Landing Platform (where Luke i sshe's preventing it from being done in the first place. armed with a lightsaber), as well as the Dark Endor sites Dark Forest and Ewok Village (both with Ewoks).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 42,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Dark targets that system using A Bright Center To The Universe (\"At locations related to target system,",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Presence",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Think of presence in the spiritual or mystical sense, as When a card uses the phrase the Force emanating from an individual. Remember Vader saying, \"I sense something. A presence I've not felt since...\" In game terms, each of your characters with ability creates a 'presence' at one location that your opponent's characters can sense (eve nwhen they are 3PO or R2 -D2 at that location (they don at the bridge, cockpit or cargo bay of an enclosed vehicle or starship).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Having presence at a location is defined as (1) having total ability of 1 or higher at that location, or (2) having a card with the Presence icon at that location. Note that this means even cards that are",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "inside of starships and enclosed vehicles",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "contribute their ability or Presence icon towards creating presence at that location. See Icons -",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A location where no player has presenc Presence Icon.",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "No card may create presence at more than one locat ion. For example, if the",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Executo",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "r is at Dantooine with Ozzel on the bridge and Vader at the",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Executor",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": ":",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Main Corridor site, then Ozzel (and the permanent pilots) create presence only at the Dantooine system, whereas Vader creates presence only at the corridor",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Here",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "site.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "See Prepositions.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Think of the term present as applying to something that is physically at a certain place (e.g., a starship can be in physical contact with the 'space' at a system location, but a character cannot). No card is considered to be means the location itself. For example, Gre present at more than one place at the same time. There are four places where a card can be present in the game:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• at a site location;",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• at a sector location;",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• at a system location; or",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• on an enclosed vehicle or starship card (at the bridge, cockpit or cargo bay) or enclosed in a prison.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For example, if Red 5 is at the Hoth system with Luke aboard, then Red 5 is present at the Hoth system and Luke is present aboard Red 5 (although Luke is at the Hoth system, he is not present at the system).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "An inactiv ecard is not considered present, except for situations where it is considered \"on table\" (e.g., a captive is present when targeted by Ice Storm).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Permanent pilots, passengers, and astromechs are present aboard their respective starship or vehicle (and are therefore \"present with\" any other cards that are also present at the bridge, cockpit, or cargo bay of that same starship or vehicle).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present versus Present With",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "When a card refers to another card being \"present,\" that applies only to the card being present at a location (even if the other card is not actually present itself).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "\"Present with\" is used to describe two (or more) cards that are present together (e.g., twocharacters on the same enclosed vehicle are present with each other, but one on and one off are not present with each other).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Where Present",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "\" where present \", that means that card must be present at its location. For example, \" Where present, cancels game text of C -3POor R2 -D2 \" on Commander Praji means that if Praji is present at a location, he cancels the game text of C -' tneed to be present there, only Praji).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Control Of A Location",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "You control a location if you have presence there and your opponent does not. Control of a location is checked whenever required, not just during the control phase. The condition is continuous, not an action.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Unoccupiede.",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "However, an undercover spy at a location prevents that location from being unoccupied.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Occupy",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A location where you have presence (regardless of",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "whether the opponent has presence there).",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "The word 'here' in game text means \"at this location,\" unle sscontext indicates otherwise. (For example, Bacta Tank, Commence Recharging and Cyborg Construct use the word 'here' to mean \"on this card.\")",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "System Location",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "When a card or rule refers to a \"system location\" it at Shot, Kid!",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "(\"Whenever you deploy a unique (•) starship to a system location, retrieve 3 Force\") will not allow you to retrieve if you deploy a starship aboard a capital starship, because it has not been deployed to the system location.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Prepositions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Prep ositions (at, on, aboard, to, with, from, in etc.) are used to express simple relationships between cards, and have their normal English language connotations.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A character, starship, vehicle, weapon, or device is \" on \" a system if it is: (1) Present at any site, cloud or Death Star IIsector related to that system name. (2) At the bridge, cockpit or cargo bay of a starship or vehicle that is present at any site, cloud or Death Star IIsector related to that system name. Thus, for example, Luke is \"on Hoth\" if he is present at the Echo Command Center, inside the Wampa Cave, or piloting Rogue 1 at the Ice Plains.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For \" on Cloud City, \" see Cloud City Locations in Chapter 9.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A character, starship, vehicle, weapon, or device is \" at \" a system if (1) it is on that planet or mobile system, (2) orbiting that system, or (3) At the bridge, cockpit or cargo bay of a starship that is present at (orbiting) that system. For example, Luke is \"at Hoth\" if he is piloting Red 5 and Red 5 is present at the Hoth system. A card that deploys so that it is \"at\" a location has deployed \" to \" said location.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 43,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A card is \" with \" another card if they are both at the same location. A card can be \" at same location \" as",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "itself, but a card cannot be \" with \" itself (see Combo Cards in Appendix Cfor an exception).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A character, starship, vehicle, weapon or device is \" aboard \" (or \" on \") a starship or vehicle if it is: (1) At any site related to that starship or vehicle. (2) At the bridge, cockpit or cargo bay of that starship or vehicle. This means that Luke would not be at Hoth if he was at the",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Home One",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": ": Docking Bay while the Star Cru iser",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Home",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Prepositions",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "One",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "was present at the Hoth system. In this case, Luke is at the",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Home One",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": ": Docking Bay, and aboard",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Home",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(or aboard) the Void Spider.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "One",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": ". Similarly, Tarkin at the Death Star: War Room while the Death Star orbits Alderaan is not \"at Alderaan\", but the Death Star is.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "See Pres ence and Present.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present, Presence And Prepositions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "These three concepts, though closely related, have very important differences in the game. As explained under the corresponding entries, think of prepositions as relational, presence as spiritual and present as • The Void Spider is present at the farm. physical. These terms overlap somewhat, and are often used together to make a card operate in a specific manner. The three concepts are easy to understand if you take them one at a time, as seen in the examples on the following page.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Alone/Lone",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Your character or permanent pilot is alone at a location if it is active and you have no other cards at that location that have ability or are characters. Combo Cards (such as Artoo & Threepio or Tonnika Sisters), and a permanent pilot of a starship or vehi cle that has system:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Millennium Falcon",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(with Han and C -3PO in the multiple permanent pilots (such as",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Executo",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "r or a TIE cockpit), Red 6 (with Jek Porkins piloting) and the Squadron), are not considered to be alone.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Your starship or vehicle is alone at a location if the only active characters, vehicles and starships you have at that location are aboard that starship or vehicle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "All Cards/All Characters",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Any game text or rule that causes \"all cards\" (or \"all characters\", etc.) to be lost, missing, captured, or otherwise leave the table will affect cards on both sides (even inactive cards), unless specifically told otherwise.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Cards with such game text includes Cantina Brawl, Thermal Detonator, Proton Bombs, Program Trap and Debris Zone. Rules include those for \"blown away\" as well as \"collapsed.\" It should be noted that an imprisoned character and a frozen captive are treated a little differently. See captives-imprisoned, Ap. C; captives-frozen, Ap. C.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Any weapon or interrupt that causes \"all cards\" to be lost (or missing, captured, or otherwise leave the table) at a location only affects characters, vehicles, starships, weapons and devices. Also, the effect on any target of an \"all cards\" situation cannot be prevented (such as Force Field trying to stop Concussion Grenade, Jerus Jannick trying to protect a leader from a Thermal Detonator, or Droid Shutdown to protect a droid from a seeker; none of the above can be used) unless it is specifically permitted (such as I Thought They Smelled Bad On The Outside protecting a character from Ice Storm), or if a card states that it can prevent such effects \"for any reason\".",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Note that this applies solely to the effect, you may still cancel weapon destinies as normal.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present, Presence And Prepositions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A Simple Example",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "If Bossk is aboard the Bespin Motors Void Spider at Tatooine: Lars' Moisture Farm, the following are true:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Bossk is at the farm, at Tatooine, on Tatooine and on",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• The Void Spider is at the farm, at (and on) Tatooine.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Presence",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Bossk creates presence at the farm.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• The Void Spider does not cre ate presence at the farm, but its permanent pilot does.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Bossk is present aboard the Void Spider.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "An important distinction in this example is that Bossk is at the farm but, because the Void Spider is encl osed, he is not present at the farm.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Present, Presence And Prepositions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A More Detailed Example",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "This example describes a complex game situation, and is provided primarily for reference. It is not necessary for most players to concern themselves with this level of detail. Assume that the Death Star is orbiting Yavin 4 and the following starships are at the Death Star",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Executor",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(with Piett on the bridge; also, Vader and Luke are at the Comm Station site, Tarkin is aboard a Lift Tube at the Comm Station and Leia is at the Main Corridor site). This example results in the following:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Prepositions",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• The characters are all on (also aboard) their respective starships.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• The Death Star is at Yavin 4, and the starships are all at the Death Star.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Han, C -3PO, Jek and Piett are all at the Death Star.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Han is at same location as C -3PO, Jek and Piett.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Vader, Tarkin, the Lift Tube and Luke are at the Comm Station site, at same location and at same site.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Tarkin is on (also aboard) the Lift Tube, and Leia is at the Main Corridor site.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 44,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Battle: A battle is initiated at the Death Star system, which means that Han, C -3PO and Jek (aboard",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Falcon",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "and Red 6) are in a battle together, against Piett and the",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Executor",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
