              "text": "Attacks"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "The following overview on the steps of a battle is comprehensive; for a more concise overview, see Battle In Brief.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Initiate The Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Because a battle is an action, it follows the normal rules of actions: meeting conditions, choosing targets, paying costs. The condition is both you and your opponent having presence at a location, and the target is that this may be modified (e.g. Wars Not Make One Great), has been initiated at that location for all purposes.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• At this time, any automatic actions triggered by the initiation will occur (e.g. Scum And Villainy).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "After all automatic actions are complete, optional responses (\" just actions \") occur. Players may play the following types of actions at this time:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Actions that play as a response to a battle being initiated, typically indicated by the phrasing \" if a",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "similar (e.g. Rapid Fire).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• The opponent of the player who initiated battle may use ' react ' game text on their cards to deploy a card as a ' react ' (e.g. Comlink or Spiral) or move a card as a ' react ' (e.g. Arcona or Blizzard Scout 1). See React, Ap. C.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "These optional responses alternate between players, the battle. The optional responses continue until both players pass consecutively, then the Weapons Segment begins.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons Segment",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "During the weapons segment, players fire weapons and perform other top level actions as outlined below.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Player salternate taking weapons segment actions, beginning with the player who initiated the battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "When both players 'pass' their top-level weapons segment actions consecutively, the weapons segment ends.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Also note:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Characters, vehicles, and starships introduced to the battle location during the weapons segment WILL participate in the battle (unless prohibited, such as due to having already battled that turn).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• If all presence is removed from either side during the weapons segment, the battle W ILL end immediately.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 53,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons Segment",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Firing Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "It is a special rule of battle that any weapons in the battle (and any long-range weapons capable of firing into the battle) may be fired once (and only once, unless specifically permitted otherwise-this applies even if the weapon is somehow on a different card during the battle than the one who fired). Weapons fired this way must target a card participating in the battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Any weapons involved in the battle may be fired one at a time; each use of a we apon is one top-level action",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "out in the following order:",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "within the battle. Each weapon describes how it works, including the kinds of cards it may target, the Force required to fire it, the destiny draw required for success and, if successful, the consequences for the target.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Most weapons specify that they 'hit' their target when successful. (Some weapons, instead of causing a 'hit,' specify some other kind of outcome.) Any 'hit' cards are turned sideways, but they still continue to participate in the battle. For example, a card that is 'hit' can still fire its • Cards introduced to the battle location during the own weapon, if it has one.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Later on in the battle, ' hit ' cards will be lost. If the battle ends prematurely, any 'hit' cards are immediately lost.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For detailed information on weapons, their use, being 'hit,' etc., see Weapons, Ch. 9.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons Segment",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Specific Actions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Most top-level actions that are specific to battling can only be played during the weapons segment. Examples of top-level weapons segment actions include:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Actions which modify or reset power without also aff ecting attrition (e.g. Black 11, Skull).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Actions which optionally modify or reset the number of battle destinies, power destinies, or attrition destinies (e.g. Haven, Skywalkers). Such actions are played now, but the destinies are not actually drawn until the power segment.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Actions which set conditions on destinies in general (not targeting specific destinies) (e.g. I Don ' t Like The player must draw all of their power destinies (there Sand, Jabba ' s Haven).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Actions which modify or reset total battle destiny are played now. Such actions schedule a change upon the total battle destiny to occur later (e.g. I ' mhow many power destinies they must draw and then With You Too, Insertion Planning, Lando ' s Not A drawing them, increasing their total power.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "System He ' s A Man).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• By default, actions which take place during battle that do not fall under any other specific timeframe (e.g. Combined Attack, Losing Track).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "See Power Segment and Damage Segment for information about actions that play during those segments instead.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons Segment",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Other Actions",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Top-level actions unrelated to the battle may also be initiated during the weapons segment (e.g. Beru Stew, Gravel Storm, or peeking at your Reserve Deck with Electrobinoculars).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Note that this is unique to the weapons segment. Very entitled to draw 0 battle destinies, but even this 0 can few types of top-level actions are eligible to be played during the power and damage segments.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 54,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "During battle, you may not initiate another battle, nor an attack.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
