              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Modifying The Number Of Destinies",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Like all modifiers, any modifiers to the number of battle destinies you draw will be either automatic or optional.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "They are handled in different ways.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Automatic destiny modifiers do not use the word \"may,\" itions are met. For example, Leia With Blaster Rifle says \"Adds one battle destiny if with Han.\" This is an",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Automatic modifiers to the number of destinies are checked immediately before you draw the first battle destiny in the power segment. In this case, Leia and Han must still be participating in the battle to use this modifier.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "for example, apply optional modifiers. Also, text such as \"May add one battle destiny\" is optional, because the choice to initiate this is up to the player. Any optional actions that are \"top level\" actions, that is, they are not responses to another action, which means they can only be initiated during the weapons segment of battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "The required initiation conditions for any optional actions are checked when that action is initiated. For example, if playing Skywalkers, the condition of Luke and Leia being in a battle together is checked at the time the interrupt is played. If the action successfully resolves, the additional draw(s) is scheduled as an automatic modifier that will occur when battle destiny is drawn. At that time, the conditions for initiating that action are not checked again. Using the Skywalkers example, if Leia was lost or captured after playing Skywalkers, the two additional destinies from Skywalkers would still be drawn.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "The cumulative rule applies to any modifiers to the number of destinies you draw, whether automatic or optional. Thus two Armored A ttack Tanks will add 2 battle destiny, not 4.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 59,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For a character, starship, vehicle, weapon, or device to add battle destiny (or destiny to power or attrition), that card must be participating in battle (unless specified otherwise). For other card types, sim ply follow the conditions on the cards themselves.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Battle Destiny",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "In Brief",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Follow this for a simplified breakdown for how many battle destiny draws you are allowed.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Step 1: Counting Start with 0.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Add 1 if you have 4 or more ability in the battle (except passengers of starships or enclosed vehicles) Add any optional modifiers that you played during the wea pon segment (such as Skywalkers) Add any automatic modifiers that are currently satisfied (such as Leia With Blaster Rifle) That number is your total: X Step 2: Prohibiting Conditions Check for any conditions such as \"ability of 6 or more required to draw battle destiny\" or \"draws no more than 1 battle destiny\" that prevent or limit your draws. If there are none, or if you meet those conditions, go to the next step. If there is at least one, and you do not meet those conditions, then X is reduced to whatever the condition states.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Step 3: Unable To Otherwise Conditions Check to see if you have any cards participating that say \"Draws Y Battle Destiny If Unable To Otherwise.\" Step 4: Total Destinies You may draw X or Ydestinies, whichever is larger.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Battle Destiny",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Example",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "For example: Light Side has Han With Heavy Blaster Pistol and Commander Luke Skywalker (V) (who is piloting Rogue 1) at Jundland Wastes. The Dark Side initiates a bat tle there; during the weapons segment Light Side plays Don't Get Cocky to add 2 battle destinies (Han and Luke are together). The Dark Side shoots Han with a Disruptor Pistol, a weapon which makes its target immediately lost, so Han goes to the Lost Pile. During the power segment, the Light Side starts with 0, adds 1 for four ability (Luke), adds 0 for automatic modifiers (Han's game text would have added a destiny with Luke if he were here now, but because he left the table he can't), adds 2 for Don't Get Cocky (because conditions were met when it was played, and are not rechecked) for a total of 3.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "However, the location states \"Total ability of 6 or more required for you to draw battle destiny here.\" Luke does not have enough ability alone, so the 3 is reduced to 0.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Now, Luke states that when he's piloting Rogue 1 he draws 2 battle destiny if not able to otherwise. Two is the larger number, thus you may draw 2 battle destiny.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "All characters, starships, vehicles, weapons, or",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "devices at the location where a battle takes place",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(whether present or not) are participating in that",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(unless they are excluded). A card is considered to be participating in a battle as soon as the battle has been initiated, or as soon as that card is intro duced to excluded from battle may not be used to allow that card the battle location as long as that card is introduced before the power segment begins. Any card introduced after the power segment has begun may never participate in that battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Even if the battle ends prematurely (or is canceled) the cards hav estill participated in a battle. Cards which participate in one battle may not normally participate in battle again during the same turn, with the following exception: a captive who has just been released will rejoin a battle they were previously particip ating in. See Captives -Releasing.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A card that fires a long-range weapon into a battle from another location is not participating in that battle for game purposes.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Any card which leaves the location of a battle immediately ceases participating in that battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "May Not Participate In Battle (Cannot Battle)",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Some game actions may restrict a card from participating in battle. A card that may not participate cannot contribute presence towards the initiation of a battle (nor can any cards on board it), nor can its game text be applied in order to initiate a battle. The game text of other cards (such as Artoo & Threepio) may not be used to initiate a battle at that location either unless there are other applicable cards there that may par ticipate in battle. If a battle is initiated at that card's location (because there are other cards that allow battle to be initiated), or a card is subject to a may not participate effect while participating in a battle, then that card is immediately excl uded from that battle. See Excluded From Battle. A card that may not participate in battle can still attack and be attacked by creatures.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Excluded From Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Excluding a card from battle removes a card from participating in the current battle in progress. Cards that are excluded from battle are considered inactive for the duration of the battle (remember that when a card is inactive, then all cards deployed on and aboard it are inactive as well); however, being excluded will not cause objectives to flip or other cards to be canceled or otherwise removed from table (these are specific exceptions to the rules). When a battle ends, all cards that were excluded from that battle are simultaneously reactivated as an automatic response to that \"battle just ended\" event. See Battle Just Ended, Ch. 6. Inactive pilots and passengers will still occupy pilot/passenger capacity slots.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Only a card currently participating in a battle is a suitable target for an exclusion action (except for cards subjected to a \"may not participate\" condition).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Inactive cards do not participate in battle (since they are not on table for such purposes); however, simply making a card inactive does not count as excluding it for the purposes of actions that prevent or a retriggered by exclusion. Likewise, leaving table does not count as exclusion. Thus, while Coruscant: Night Club prevents Han from being excluded, he can still be captured, missing, lost, taken into hand, or sent to the Used Pile.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "However, game text that prevents a card from being to participate in more than one battle per turn.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 60,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "This phrase is equivalent to participating in battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "In A Battle Together/In Battle With/Involved In The Same Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Two or more characters are \"in a battle together\" if they are participating in the same battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "During Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "All characters, starships, vehicles, weapons, or devices that can perform an action \"during battle\" (or provide an automatic modifier or otherwise alter the game state in some way \"during battle\") only can be used if that card is participating in battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Interrupts that indicate that they are played only during and 'cloaks' (it doesn't particip battle (by use of language such as \"during battle\" or \"if a battle was just initiated\", etc) require their appropriate targets to be participating in that battle unless indicated otherwise.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Examples",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Sergeant Wallen deploys as a react to a battle; he is participating in battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Panic deploys a starship to the system where a battle is taking place; the starship is participating in battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A battle destiny draw triggers Tauntaun Bones, allowing Light to deploy a character imme diately for free. Since the power segment has begun, the character is not participating in the battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A captive is released during the damage segment of a battle after his escort is forfeited, moving to the Light side of the location. He is not participating in battle.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Luke is forfeited during battle; he immediately ceases participating in that battle. Old Ben is used to return him to the site; he is still not participating in the battle (because he returned after the power segment began).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating I n Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Excluded",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Example 1",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "At the start of the damage segment, check all cards that Leia With Blaster Rifle (\"Adds one battle destiny if with Han.\") and Han (V) are at the Battle Plains. Dark deploys Blizzard 1, and then General Veers aboard it.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Light responds to the playing of Veers with Rebel Barrier (\"Use 1 Force to prevent any character or starship just deployed by the opponent from battling or moving for the remainder of this turn.\"). Dark now deploys Snoova and a Vibro-ax on him (\"Target immediately excluded from battle if...\").",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Dark initiates battle; Veers is excluded as an automatic action (he is now inactive). Because there are no other pilots aboard, Blizzard 1 is unpiloted for this battle. Dark takes the first action and targets Han with the ax, and wins the draw. Han is now excluded and thus inact ive. immunity to attrition from more than one source, it Leia fires at Snoova and misses. With no further actions the power segment begins. Light gets 1 battle destiny for having four ability there, but does not add 1 for Leia being with Han (because Han is inactive and thus not there); his draw is 2 and to tal power is 5. Dark gets no destiny (Veers' ability is not applied because he's inactive) so his total is 7. Light loses 2 Force from hand to cover the battle damage. Dark loses Snoova to cover the attrition (he could have chosen Blizzard 1, which even unpiloted was still participating, which would have caused Veers to be lost as well. Veers couldn't be forfeited because he was inactive). With the damage segment completed the battle ends and Han and Veers are no longer inactive.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Excluded",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Example 2",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Dark plays Imperial Barrier on Luke, and Light battles (Light has another character present that may participate in battles). Luke will be excluded as an automatic action when the battle begins. Although Light initiated the battle, if a card were to check which player excluded Luke, the answer would be Dark (his Imperial Barrier card excluded Luke).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Excluded",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Example 3",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Dark has Maul piloting Maul's Sith Infiltrator at Kessel, ate in battles). A battle occurs there (Dark has other ships present). Maul ' s Sith Infiltrator is immediately excluded, becoming inactive.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Maul also becomes inactive (because cards on an inactive card are also inactive). If a card were to check whether Maul is \" excluded from battle \", the answer would be no. Maul is not excluded, just inactive.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Participating In Battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "During Battle Example",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "4 -LOM (\"Once during each battle, if present with Zuckuss, may use 1 Force to search any Used Pile and relocate one character there to the lost pile.\") is present with Zuckuss at the Cantina. A battle occurs at Kessel.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Dark cannot use 4 -LOM's ability because he isn't participating in the battle at Kessel.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Immune To Attrition",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Some characters, vehicles ands tarships are protected from varying levels of attrition (written as \"immune to attrition < 5\"). When forfeiting cards to satisfy attrition, you are not required to forfeit any card that has this immunity (unless the total attrition is greater than the card 'simmunity level).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "list immunity to attrition, and compare that to the current attrition against you. Any cards with an immunity number greater than that are unaffected by attrition this battle (you do not have to forfeit them); all others are affected. After this is done it cannot be changed for this battle (i.e., you can't recheck it again later to see if immunity had changed, such as Luke Skywalker, Jedi Knight having his immunity increased when he's alone).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "An enclosed vehicle or starship with immunity to attrition protects itself and all cards aboard the bridge, cockpit, or cargo bay (it does not protect cards at related starship or vehicle sites).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Immunity is not cumulative; thus,",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "if a card is granted",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "benefits only from the highest such immunity. Any card which is immune to attrition may still be voluntarily forfeited to satisfy attrition or battle damage.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 61,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Immune To Attrition",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Gaining And Losing",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Whenever an action or game text that grants immunity to attrition is in conflict with an action or game text that removes immunity to attrition, the removing action overrides the gaining action. For example, the Light Side player has Sometimes I Amaze Even Myself on table, causing all Imperials to lose their immunity to attrition. Thus a Stormtrooper alone at the (Dark Side) Yavin 4: Jungle still has no immunity. In a battle there, if the dark side plays Trooper Assault it will provide a",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 62,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "power bonus to the Stormtrooper, but will not provide that trooper with any attrition immunity.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 62,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Remember that you cannot lose something that does not exist (see Implied Target Rule, Ch. 1), so you may not initiate an action that results in losing immunity to attrition if you do not have immunity.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
