            {
              "text": "If a card is has one dot (•) it is considered 'unique' and if it has two or more dots (e.g. ••) it is considered 'restricted'. The number of dots restricts: (a) the number of cards of that title that are allowed on table at any given time, and (b) the number of cards of that title and persona that may be played or deployed each turn (even if one is canceled, returned to hand, if it has already resolved and been placed in the Used Pile or Lost Pile, etc). Some unique or restricted cards are available to both sides of the Force (such as •Ice Storm), but this restriction is still applicable, regardless of the fact that it is being played by a different player.",
