          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Foreign Languages",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "To ensure consistent tournament play worldwide, one language (English) is used as the standard for all game play. Cards and rules printed in other languages are played and interpreted exactly the same as their English-language counterparts (and according to all current rulings, errata and clarifications). For example, See Movement, Ch. 7. an English copy of Vader's Lightsaber (from Premiere) and a Japanese foil copy (from Reflections III) are considered to have the same card title for all game play purposes (e.g. uniqueness rules, Grimtaash, etc.).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 77,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Alternate Image Cards",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "An alternate image card set is two or more cards with identical title, game text, lore, statistics etc., but with differing pictures. Since card identity is determined by title, they are considered the same.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 77,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Also, these cards may be marked by a gold ring around the expansion icon. This does not change the expansion icon in any way (thus you may not persona replace Queen Amidala, Ruler Of Naboo with an alternate image Queen Amidala, Ruler Of Naboo).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 77,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Spelling Errors / Typos",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "On rare occasions a card or rule may contain a spelling or typographical error, such as C -3PO being spelled as C -3P0. Such errors have no gameplay imp act; the card exceptions, see Presence Icon). Droids without armor or rule should be played as though the word was spelled correctly.",
