            {
              "text": "• Creatures that attach to starsh ips will immediately detach when it becomes a vehicle, and vice versa.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 81,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Devices and Effects (of any kind) which use a clause of their deployment text to deploy on and/or target a double-sided card as a starship, are lost when it becomes a vehicle (unless that same deployment clause can also target vehicles) and vice versa. Ignore any other deployment requirements of the Device or Effect when flipping.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 81,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "In addition, the owner of the card may only utilize an optional 'flipping' mechanic a total of one time per turn, regardless of which side of the card it was initiated from. Note that even if the card is on table as a landed starfighter (and therefore unpiloted) or as an unpiloted vehicle, any text related to flipping the card is still considered active. Also, i nrare cases, after flipping this card it may be possible for it to be aboard a starship without appropriate capacity for it (no available starfighter or vehicle slots). In these situations the card would be lost (which will typically result in it being relocated somewhere else, such as out of play).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 81,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Effects",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Type of card that represents long-term alterations to other cards or aspects of the game. There are six different kinds, or subtypes, of Effects: Effects, Immediate Effects, Mobile Effects, Utinni Effects, Political Effects and Starting Effects. A card tha ttargets 'Effects' (or an Effect) targets only the first subtype of Effect (it is not targeting the card type Effect), not the other five, unless it specifically mentions one or more of",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 82,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "the others. Game text that targets an \"Effect of any kind\" can target any subtype of Effect.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 82,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Effects",
