            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "You may fire a weapon only when a card or rule permits you to fire. Simply follow the rules of firing listed under Firing (and anything the card or rule might add).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For example, you are permitted by rule to use a weapon",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Artillery",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "during battle. When you do this, you must obey the normal rules of firing; in addition, there are two special rules for firing during battle:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "you must also only target a card that is participating in the battle and you may",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "weapon, you must have your own power source",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "attempt to fire each weapon only once per battle",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": ". power droid or any fusion generator) present. The Hoth:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Just Fired",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A weapon is considered to have been 'just fired' after the firing action has completed all 3 steps successfully and the firing action is coming off the stack. If a weapon firing action is canceled or prevented from resolving throughout this process, then that weapon cannot be considered to have been 'just fired.'",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Using Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Examples",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Firing During Battle:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Dutch piloting Rogue 1 and Luke are in a battle with Boba Fett With Blaster Rifle, who has captured Leia With Blaster Rifle. Han With Heavy Blaster Pistol has been excluded from battle, Chewie With Blaster Rifle is missing, and Lando With Vibro -Ax is undercover.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "During the battle Boba Fett wants to fire his weapon; he meets conditions (he's in a battle). He chooses his target, which must be Luke (because Han, Leia, Chewie, and Lando are not participating in the battle, and Dutch is not present with the weapon). He pays his cost (free). He draws and gets a 5, which is more than enough to hit. Luke is turned sideways (he'll be lost during the damage segment). None of Light's cards may fire because all the cards with weapons are inactive.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Firing Using A Card:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Han armed with Han's Heavy Blaster Pistol (V) uses its text to fire during Light's control phase. He meets conditions (the weapon's game text). He targets an pays the cost (1 Force). He draws destiny, and hits; the spy is immediately lost (resolve weapon fire).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Using Weapons Several Times Per Turn:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Obi -Wan armed with his lightsaber (\"Deploy on Obi -Wan. May add 1 to Force drain where present. May target a character or creature for free. Draw two destiny. Target hit, and its forfeit = 0, if total destiny > defe nse value.\") is present at the Cantina with Vader.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Light plays Sorry About The Mess and Obi -Wan targets Vader. He has met conditions (the interrupt permits firing), has chosen his target (who is present with the weapon) and he pays the cost (it's free): thus he draws 2 destiny, which totals 8. Vader is hit, and thus immediately lost. Obi -Wan now controls the site, so Light Force drains there. Obi -Wan may use that lightsaber to modify the Force drain (because it isn't a continuous modifier, but an optional one, it counts as using the weapon, so had Obi -Wan fired a different weapon, he couldn't modify the Force drain with his lightsaber). Light then uses the movement text of Mos Eisley to move Obi -Wan there where Dengar is present.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "During his battle phase Lig htstarts a battle there. Obi -Wan may swing his lightsaber at Dengar as well, but may do so only once (because weapons can only be fired once per battle).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 94,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A kind of weapon which is deployed on a site. Unlike most other weapons, artiller yweapons usually have deploy and forfeit boxes.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "To fire your artillery",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(a",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Main Power Generators site and the virtual card Captain Yutani With Blaster Cannon also say that they can power Light Side artillery weapons. An artillery weapon may not be moved unless specified otherwise. permitted to deploy, the card may deploy regardless of When an artillery weapon is fired by a character (even if using an Artillery Remote) it counts to wards the number of weapons that character may use in a turn. Thus a character using an E-web Blaster may not use a Blaster Rifle in the same turn.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Automated",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A kind of weapon which activate themselves. Since they deploy on bounty hunters, Jawas, Han, etc. and thus do are automatic, you do not need a character, vehicle, etc. to fire them. Most automated weapons specify when they are used within their game text. Automated starship (unless specifically allowed to by the card weapons can only target cards present with them, and that includes when checking for triggering conditions such as those on Vehicle Mine. Unlike other weapons, automated weapons are not fired. The lone exception to this is Laser Projector, which may be fired during battle like any other weapon. Cards that allow you to fire a weapon outside of the battle phase (for example Sniper, Sorry About The Mess, Blasted Droid or Suppressive Fire) may only be used to fire a Laser Projector.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "The destiny draw for automated weapons is still considered a weapon destiny, except for Timer Mine.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Seekers are a special type of automated weapon (see Seekers).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "For information on mines, see Mining Droid Rules, Ap. C.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Character Weapon",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A kind of weapon that deploys on a character (it may",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "only be used by that character).",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapon",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Mobile System Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A weapon deployed on a mobile system (or Trench) is considered present at its location, and may fire according to the normal rules of firing.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Starship And Vehicle Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "A kind of weapon that deploys on a starship or vehicle (it may only be used by that starship or vehicle).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Your starships and vehicles may fire weapons so long as they are piloted (or driven). This counts as the starship or vehicle firing, not the characters or permanent pilots on board, even if the weapon's game text mentions that a character is required in order to target with it (thus, a Nikto alone on a Skiff may use his Mos Eisley Blaster the same turn the Skiff fires an Antipersonnel Laser Cannon).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Starship Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Special Deployment",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Some starships have game text allowing weapons with certain attrib utes to deploy on them. Such weapons can only be deployed if they can deploy (by the weapon's own game text) on another starship of the same type (capital or starfighter). For example, you may deploy Quad Laser Cannons on Nebulon -B Frigate because the cann on may deploy on Corellian Corvettes; but not X -Wing Laser Cannons because those only deploy on starfighters. Likewise you may deploy Boosted TIE Cannon on a TIE Defender because it deploys on a type of starfighter, but not Laser Cannon Batteries because that weapon only deploys on capital starships.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Note that if a card is mentioned by name as being its game text (e.g., Ion Cannon on",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "IG",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-2000).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Deploying And Carrying",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Each weapon (and device) specifies who or what it may be deployed on and what the deploy cost is (if any).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Although many character weapons specify that they deploy only on warriors, other character weapons not require a warrior. You may not deploy weapons or devices on your opponent's character, vehicle, or itself).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Although you are restricted in the number of weapons and devices you may use in a turn, you may still deploy as many on an appropriate card as you like. If a weapon can deploy on a card, then that card may use that weapon. However, the reverse is not true-just because a character may use a particular weapon does not mean that that weapon can be deployed on them (see Aurra Sing). Some characters, such as Kabe and RA -7, have game text that allows them to carry weapons that they cannot use. While a card is carrying a weapon or device they cannot use, that weapon or device is inactive (this does not apply to 'extra' weapons a character might be armed with after he uses a particular weapon on a turn, only to weapons that a character can never normally use).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Transferring",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "During your deploy phase, you may transfer your weapon (or device) from one of your characters, vehicles, or starships to another such card present with the targeted character, vehicle, or starship on which the weapon is currently deployed by using Force equal to the deploy cost of the weapon (or device) and obeying all relevant deployment restr ictions. (e.g. you cannot transfer Vader's Lightsaber to Obi -Wan, or a Cloud City Blaster to a character not on Cloud City).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Destiny Any destiny drawn when firing a weapon",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "(different from battle destiny). Drawing weapon destiny is mandatory once you fire the weapon (meaning you may not fire the weapon if you do not have at least one card in your Reserve Deck). If the weapon specifies more than one destiny draw, you must draw the required number. See 1.F. Destiny, Ch. 1.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "A weapon destiny draw is considered to be \"at\" the location of the weapon. Thus for any location text that says \"Your weapon destinies here are +1\", it refers to any weapons at that site (even if the target is at another location).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 95,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Unless otherwise specified, any modifier applied to destiny when firing a weapon is applied to the TOTAL weapon destiny, and NOT to any individual weapon destiny draw. Note that this is AFTER each individual draw has been compl eted (and thus after any individual weapon destinies that were negative are reset to 0). (see Section F. Drawing Destiny)",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Firing For Free",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Sometimes a weapon is permitted to fire for free, such as with the card Stay Sharp. In those cases, if any variables depend on the cost of firing, the value for that variable is 0. For example, if Stay Sharp! was used to fire X -Wing Laser Cannons, Xwould be 0 and thus provide no bonus to hitting the target.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "See Repeating Weapons.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Firing Separately Or Combined",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Sometimes you are permitted to fire a weapon more than once and do so either separately or combined. In these instances (not in instances where you can fire more than once, such as Maul's Double-bladed specifically able to do so (e.g., R5 Lightsaber, but only when you may do so \"sepa rately or Extinguisher), or the target leaves play. The phrase \"all combined\" such as Targeting Computer), do the following: declare that you are firing twice, and then declare whether you are firing separately or combined.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Both shots fired will be considered part of the same overall action, so no top-level actions may take place between shots. If firing separately, choose the first target, and resolve, then choose a target again (it may be the same target) and resolve.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If firing combined, treat each firing as a single weapon destiny (not a weapon destiny total, even if multiple draws are made), then add them together to form the total weapon destiny, apply further modifiers to total weapon destiny, and then resolve.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "hit",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "The act or state of having been successfully shot by",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "any weapon thats pecifies \"target hit\" in its game text.",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Hit cards are marked by turning the card sideways until the damage segment of the battle, at which time the target must be forfeited. If the battle ends before the damage segment, then \"hit\" cards are immediately lost.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Any card \"hit\" but not participating in a battle or an attack (e.g., a weapon is fired using an Interrupt such as Sniper, or the character is excluded) is immediately lost. It should be noted that any other weapon effect besides \"hit\" (e.g., captured, forfeit = 0, lost) is applied immediately upon resolution of the weapon destiny draw.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If a successful weapon firing has multiple results (such as \"target hit and opponent loses 2 force\" or \"target hit and is forfeit=0\"), and one of those results is for the target to be hit, then anything that prevents the target from being hit also prevents all of the other results.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "\"hit targets are immediately lost\"",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "The phrase \"Any 'hit' targets are immediately lost\" applies only to weapons which actually 'hit' targets.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Permanent Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Other weapons have their normal result.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Instead Of Firing",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Some cards permit you to use a certain modifier or action \"instead of firing\" a weapon (such as End This Destructive Conflict or Precise Hit). To perform such actions, you must target your weapon that would be capable of being fired during that timeframe and has an applicable target (you do not have to have the Force to fire it, merely the ability). That weapon is now treated as having been used (not fired), so that it counts towards the number of times that weapon may be fired, and counts towards the number of weapons the character, vehicle, or starship may use per turn (X -Wing Assault Squadron may fire only 2 more, IG -88 may fire only one more, and A -Wing may not fire any).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Ion Weapons",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "An ion weapon conceptually disables electronic circuitry and mechanical systems of starships and droids, but does not cause a target to be 'hit.' The results of an ion weapon are immediate. Most ion weapons are ion cannons, which can reset power, armor, maneuver and/or hyperspeed to zero (see unmodifiable values).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "This reset lasts until the target is repaired by a card-D4, R5 -A2, Fire weapons aboar dtarget are lost\" refers only to weapons the targeted starship can use (i.e., starship weapons deployed on the starship, not weapons deployed on other cards inside the starship).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 96,
