              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 97,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If the game text of a card with a permanent weapon is canceled or suspended, that card is still considered to be in possession of the weapon that is specified within its game text; theuniqueness of that weapon still applies, but that character, vehicle, or starship is incapable of utilizing the weapon's text. 'Scanning' or copying the game text of a card with a permanent weapon, and the scanning card is not considered to possess that weapon. ' Scanning' or copying the game text of a card with a to use that weapon, and the scanning card is not considered to possess that weapon.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 97,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Cards that modify, reset, or otherwise change the destiny number, deploy cost, or forfeit value of a specific type of weapon (e.g., a blaster, bowcaster or lightsaber) have no impact on cards with permanent weapons.",
