        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Artwork Cards",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Some cards, such as Thrawn Pincer, may refer to artwork cards. Artwork cards are defined by the game text of the Effect card Thrawn's Art Collection.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Artwork cards are stacked on Thrawn's Art Collection and are in a Supporting state. Anything that targets \"artwork cards on table\" (or similar phrasing) will target these stacked cards.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Asteroid Rules",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Wherever 'Asteroid Rules' are in effect, your starships present there continuously risk being hit by asteroids.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "During each of your control phases, for each ship you have at an asteroid sector: 1) Opponent draws one asteroid destiny. If this card is itself a nasteroid sector, the starship is immediately lost, no matter how high its armor or maneuver. 2) Add 1 for each additional sector at that system that has 'Asteroid Rules' in effect. 3) If total asteroid destiny > armor or maneuver, the starship is lost.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Aste roid Rules",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "-",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Asteroid Destiny",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Drawing asteroid destiny against your ship is a mandatory action for your opponent. As such, your opponent chooses the target for each draw (before the draw is actually made).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Blown Away",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Certain cards will cause locations to be 'blown away.' Being blown away is a major event that will have repercussions for the rest of the game. Whenever a location is blown away, it is turned face down (Note that a blown away location is a special kind of supporting card, since it is functioning as a location; the rules in this section supersede the rules regarding card states).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "From this point on, the location cannot be deployed or converted again. It is considered an unnamed location (i.e. a blown away Alderaan cannot have Haven deployed on it) with no printed Force icons, no printed game text, and no other attributes except those specified below. Cards may still deploy and move to the location as normal (obeying all standard rules, e.g. having presence or Force icons).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If the blown away locat ion is a site:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• Any cards at the site are lost.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• If the site was previously collapsed, it no longer collapsed.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• It is considered exterior, is a part of that system, and retains its marker number (if applicable).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "If the blown away location is a system:",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 157,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "• All rel ated sites, Cloud sectors, and Death Star IIsectors (and any cards on them) are lost.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
