            {
              "text": "Characteristics",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "In addition to common attributes (e.g., deploy cost, ability, icons), many characters have additional features called characteristics (e.g., leader, stormtrooper, Wookiee).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Only Characters have characteristics.",
              "bold": true,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 177,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Characteristics are printed in the lore of the character (in addition to the normal means of having it, such as by having it in the name, subtype, or game text).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 177,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Characters may also gain characteristics from other",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 178,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "cards (for instance, Agents Of Black Sun makes certain characters a Black Sun agent).",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 178,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "Below is the list of characteristics. It must be on this list to qualify as a characteristic. Thus, Thul Fain is not an Imperial, WE D -9 -M1 'Bantha' Droid is not a bantha, and Gray Squadron Y-wing Pilot is not a Y -Wing. Note that, guards in addition to those characteristics. Specialized with the exception of infantry battle droid, droid-specific guard characteristics are: references are not on this list; this is because droids are typically referred to by subtype To determine if a card has a characteristic, see The Rule Of Three.",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "pageRef": 178,
          "textRuns": [
            {
              "text": "accountant Jedi Council member admiral leader assassin mercenary Black Sun agent miner bounty hunter musician captain Padawan clone pirate commander Resistance Agent Crimson Dawn Royal Naboo Security gambler scavenger gangster scoundrel general scout guard* senator* gunner slaver handmaiden smuggler Imperial Council member species* Infantry battle droid spy information broker tax collector Inquisitor thief insurgent Trade Federation ISB Agent trooper*",
